==English==
===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Napoleon}}

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr}} given name {{term|lang=fr|Napoléon}}, usually in reference to [[w:Napoleon Bonaparte|Napoleon Bonaparte]]. In reference to coins, via {{etyl|fr}} slang {{term|napoléon|lang=fr}}, from the appearance of Napoleon's face on the obverse of the original coins.<ref>"[http://www.oed.com/view/Entry/258537 Napoleon, ''n.¹'']" in the ''Oxford English Dictionary'' (2003), Oxford: Oxford University Press.</ref> In reference to guns and possibly cards, in reference to [[w:Napoleon III|Napoleon III]].

